    "created_at": "2016-07-19T16:03:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-19T16:03:18Z",
    "body": "> @domenic if the browsing context is discarded, is the WindowProxy disconnected from the document?\n\nInteresting. Per spec (including this update), I don't believe so. Let's say user code held on to the document object. Then the graph is:\n- user code -> document -> browsing context (via defaultView) -> WindowProxy\n- user agent -> browsing context -> WindowProxy\n\nDiscarding the browsing context breaks the user agent -> browsing context link, but does not break the user code -> document link, and thus everything in that chain is not collectable yet.\n\nHowever, http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4336 reveals that browsers generally seem to get rid of the document -> browsing context link, although of course again all in non-interoperable ways. Let me push another commit to try to address that...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/233681313/reactions",
